  "notes": "Where the 4% Health and Education Cess goes. The cess is levied on income tax plus surcharge and, unlike ordinary tax, is earmarked: its proceeds are credited to three reserve funds in the Public Account and may finance only the schemes those funds carry. This section exists because that earmark is the one thing a taxpayer can be told about their cess with any precision. It is 2025-26 revised estimates because Statement 15 publishes nothing else — the government does not report actuals for cess utilisation, which is why this is a separate section and never reconciled against the expenditure years."
}
